   "evidence": "The opposite direction exists as its own lemma, `TopCat/Limits/Basic.lean:74` (`IsCoherentWith (range ... c.\u03b9.app j)` from `IsColimit`). A grep for `IsCoherentWith` under `TauCeti/Topology/Category` finds no lemma for the coherent-to-colimit direction. `liftCoherent` is also applied by hand at Tower.lean:156 and 165.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/Homotopy/Extension/Tower.lean",
   "fix": "Factor out the sequence functor and cocone as a definition, and `hcY` as a named lemma (e.g. `TopCat.isColimitOfIsCoherentWith`) next to `TopCat.isCoherentWith_range_\u03b9_of_isColimit`. Then derive the theorem from it.",
   "issue": "The construction of `G`, `cY`, `h\u03c6`, `desc`, `hdesc` and `hcY` (about 20 lines) proves inline the general fact that a space with the topology coherent with an increasing exhausting sequence `A k` is the TopCat colimit of the inclusions `A k \u2192 A (k+1)`. That reusable fact is hidden inside one theorem.",
